    "top_frame": "Late rallies are becoming this team's only reliable signature.",
    "what_this_means": "Jackson Merrill's eighth-inning home run broke a 3\u20133 tie, and the Padres found just enough in the final two frames to beat Miami 5\u20133. Manny Machado drove in three runs, keeping the lineup relevant through five innings of one-run baseball. The bullpen. Matsui, Peralta, Morejon, and Mason Miller closing it out. Gave up nothing after the second. This was not a dominant performance. This was a team that got one clean inning when it mattered and did not waste it. They are now three straight wins deep, each one by a single run, and the pattern is becoming unmissable: early deficit, middle-inning grind, late conversion. The gap on the division shrinks by one game. The margin stays the same.",
